n2. \"BSF-1214 Torsion base with HBM PW15AHC3MR load cell\"\n3. \"BSG-99 Torsion base with Vishay 1130 load cell\"\n4. \"BSG-1214 Torsion base with Vishay 1130 load cell\"\n5. \"1824 Diamond base with Avery Weigh-Tronix FLS R60 load cell\"\n6. \"2020 Diamond base with Avery Weigh-Tronix FLS or FLS R60 load cell\"\n7. \"2424 Diamond base with Avery Weigh-Tronix FLS or FLS R60 load cell\"\n\nEach table: columns as defined, column_units, rows.\n\nFootnotes: [] → omit field entirely.\n\nComponents — also the indicator ZQ375 \"fully described in R76/2006-GB1-12.04\". Add characteristic \"described_in_certificate\": \"R76/2006-GB1-12.04\".\n\nInterfaces could be a component-level? No, keep in description.\n\ncertified_type.description — combine: family description, main features, devices, interfaces, software protection.\n\nLet me draft description: \"Family of instruments designated ZQ375 Checkweigher, comprising Torsion base (BSF/BSG) and Diamond base (BS) models. Class III, mains or battery-powered, self-indicating non-automatic weighing instruments, not designed for direct sales to the public. Main features: ZQ375 indicating device (described in R76/2006-GB1-12.04), BSF/BSG Torsion or BS Diamond base stainless steel load receptor, stainless steel column, optional ZQ-BAT battery box, optional ZQ-OPTO interface box (with or without beacon assembly). Devices: semi-automatic zero setting (≤ 4% Max), zero tracking (≤ 4% Max), semi-automatic subtractive tare, pre-set tare, recall of gross indication when tare is active, determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, checking of display, printing, PLUs, alibi storage, gravity compensation, real time clock, command via external device (PC), and checkweighing applications Sim375, Mid375, Adv375, Per375, Grad375. Interfaces: load cell 4-wire or 6-wire shielded connection, logic level inputs, open collector outputs, current loop, RS232/422/485, 10/100 Ethernet, USB host, USB device, wireless LAN 802.11b/g, ZQ-BAT battery pack, ZQ-OPTO interface box. Software designated AWT30-500161 version 1.x.x.x or 2.x.x.x; calibration and legally relevant parameters protected via physical jumper or password with incrementing counters.\"\n\nGood.\n\nrecommendation: {\"id\": \"R76\", \"edition\": 2006, \"amendment\": null, \"accuracy_classes\": [\"III\"]}. Should amendment be null or omitted? Include null or omit. I'll omit amendment? Schema lists it; null is fine. Also scheme: maybe omit at recommendation level to avoid confusion; or include \"B\". I'll include scheme: \"B\" both places? The certificate-level scheme B is MAA. For recommendation.scheme — the original R76/2006 test... I'll include scheme \"B\" in certificate only, and in recommendation omit scheme. Hmm schema shows recommendation.scheme — optional. Omit.\n\nWait, one more check: \"OIML R 76 - Edition 2006(E)\". edition: 2006.\n\nNow the certificate number: the doc header \"OIML Certificate № R76/2006-GB1-12.05 Revision 2\". number: \"R76/2006-GB1-12.05\". Fine.\n\nAlso maybe include \"revision\": \"2\"? Not in schema; revision_history covers it.\n\nPage_total: I said 5. Let me double-check markdown: \"This certificate includes 5 pages\" — repeated on every page. Yes, 5.\n\nOne more consideration: category — \"Non-Automatic Weighing Instrument\" vs \"Checkweigher\". I'll use \"Non-Automatic Weighing Instrument (Checkweigher)\".\n\nmodule_designation: \"Not applicable\" (complete instrument). OK.\n\ntype_designations: [\"ZQ375\"] — maybe also \"ZQ375 Checkweigher\". Keep [\"ZQ375\"].\n\nLet me now write final JSON carefully. It'll be long. Ensure numbers not strings, decimal points correct (59.5, 58.33, 0.8, 0.5).\n\nµV: unit_symbol \"µV\" — use \"µV\" (micro sign) or \"uV\"? I'll use \"µV\".\n\nΩ: \"Ω\".\n\nAlso for \"maximum_number_of_scale_intervals\" 6000 — unit null (intervals are dimensionless) or \"intervals\"? Use \"e\" ... no. null, maybe unit_symbol \"intervals\"? Hmm, keep null. Actually \"n max = 6000\" — dimensionless